This licence covers the code and the derived results in this archive only.

It does NOT cover the three audited datasets. Harvard-GDP, Harvard-GF and
Harvard-FairVision are third-party resources distributed by the Harvard
Ophthalmology AI Laboratory under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-
NoDerivatives 4.0 (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0). They are not redistributed here: no image,
no visual-field vector, and no bulk table of their contents appears in this
archive. Two files carry the minimal per-eye fields without which our arithmetic
could not be checked at all, and we name them so that the boundary is explicit:

  results/07_leakage_5seeds/leakage_eval_set.csv
      For the 295 eyes common to Harvard-GF and the Harvard-FairVision test
      split: the file identifier, the racial group, the binary glaucoma label,
      and our model's scores. The label and the group are the ground truth the
      reported areas under the curve are computed against.

  results/01_link_gf_fairvision/matches_gf_fv.csv and matches_gdp_fv.csv
      Matched file identifiers with the racial group and the designated split.
      These columns are already public in the article's online supplement
      (fv_census_pairs.xlsx).

Everything else under results/ is our own computed output. To re-run the stages
that need the datasets themselves, download them from their official
repositories; see the README.
